-   **Field-ordering invariant (load-bearing).** In every sidecar the `score:` field (when present) MUST precede the `defect_class:` field, and `defect_class:` MUST appear LAST among the YAML frontmatter fields. The ordering is a security invariant against duplicate-key YAML parser drift: pyyaml-style "last value wins" parsers used by future cluster-analysis tooling would let a malformed `defect_class:` value containing an injected `score:` (or any other recognized key) on a subsequent line silently override real values that came earlier. Putting `defect_class:` last bounds the blast radius — nothing the value carries on follow-on lines can shadow a load-bearing field above it. Today's `scripts/verifier-fan-in.sh` already exits on the FIRST `score:` match, so the invariant is doubly enforced; future tooling adopting a real YAML parser inherits the same guarantee.
